{"step_index":1600,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T01:19:57Z","content":"There it is. At 2M scale, the Python dict lookup shows P99 at 1.25μs — that's the hash table growing past L1 cache. Anthony called it: this is an architecture problem. The fix is sharding. Let me implement the sharded gate and prove it holds sub-microsecond at 2M.","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Shard the identity table across CPU cores so each gate lookup hits a local shard that fits in L1/L2 cache, keeping P99 sub-microsecond at 2M nodes","EndLine":86,"Instruction":"Replace the flat _IDENTITY_TABLE and gate_check with a sharded identity table that partitions across CPU cores, keeping each shard small enough to stay in L1/L2 cache","ReplacementContent":"# Master key loaded once at process boot. Read-only from below, write-only from above.\n_MASTER_KEY = os.environ.get(\n    \"XORAS_GATE_KEY\",\n    \"XORAS_SOVEREIGN_7TH_LAYER_IMMUTABLE_KEY_2026\"\n).encode(\"utf-8\")\n\n# Shard configuration — partition the identity space across CPU cores.\n# Each shard is a small dict that fits in L1/L2 cache.\n# At 2M agents / 10 shards = 200K entries per shard ≈ 12MB per shard (well within L2).\n_NUM_SHARDS = max(1, os.cpu_count() or 1)\n\n# Sharded identity table: list of dicts, indexed by shard number.\n# Each agent maps to exactly one shard via the first 4 bytes of its hash.\n_IDENTITY_SHARDS: list[Dict[str, bytes]] = [{} for _ in range(_NUM_SHARDS)]\n\n\ndef _compute_identity_hash(agent_id: str) -> bytes:\n    \"\"\"Constant-time HMAC-SHA256 of agent identity. One call, one result.\"\"\"\n    return hmac.new(_MASTER_KEY, agent_id.encode(\"ascii\"), hashlib.sha256).digest()\n\n\ndef _shard_index(identity_hash: bytes) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Constant-time shard selection: first 4 bytes of hash mod shard count.\"\"\"\n    return struct.unpack(\"<I\", identity_hash[:4])[0] % _NUM_SHARDS\n\n\ndef boot_identity_table(agent_ids: list[str]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Pre-compute all identity hashes at boot time, distributed across shards.\n    Called ONCE during system startup. After this, shards are read-only.\n    No disk I/O, no database, no network — pure in-memory sharded hash table.\n    \"\"\"\n    global _IDENTITY_SHARDS\n    _IDENTITY_SHARDS = [{} for _ in range(_NUM_SHARDS)]\n    for aid in agent_ids:\n        h = _compute_identity_hash(aid)\n        shard = _shard_index(h)\n        _IDENTITY_SHARDS[shard][aid] = h\n\n\ndef gate_check(agent_id: str, presented_token: bytes) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    THE GATE. Constant-time. One shard lookup, one comparison, pass or kill.\n\n    Args:\n        agent_id: The agent claiming identity.\n        presented_token: HMAC-SHA256 token the agent presents at activation.\n\n    Returns:\n        True = agent passes through the wall, paint sticks.\n        False = agent killed at the door. Never reaches compute.\n\n    Architecture:\n        1. Compute shard index from presented_token (constant-time, no branching).\n        2. Look up agent_id in the local shard (small dict, cache-hot).\n        3. compare_digest (constant-time, no timing leaks).\n    \"\"\"\n    shard = _shard_index(presented_token)\n    expected = _IDENTITY_SHARDS[shard].get(agent_id)\n    if expected is None:\n        return False\n    return hmac.compare_digest(expected, presented_token)\n\n\ndef generate_activation_token(agent_id: str) -> bytes:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generate the activation token an agent presents at the gate.\n    Called by the boot sequence when painting the agent's persona.\n    The agent receives this token but cannot forge it without the master key.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _compute_identity_hash(agent_id)","StartLine":29,"TargetContent":"# Master key loaded once at process boot. Read-only from below, write-only from above.\n_MASTER_KEY = os.environ.get(\n    \"XORAS_GATE_KEY\",\n    \"XORAS_SOVEREIGN_7TH_LAYER_IMMUTABLE_KEY_2026\"\n).en