{"step_index":1608,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T01:22:10Z","thinking":"**Constructing Native Gate Library**\n\nI'm now focused on building the native gate library. I plan to implement it in C or Zig, using `clang` or `zig` compilers with optimization flags for Apple M4 silicon. The core data structure will be a cache-aligned hash map. I'm considering open addressing with quadratic probing or Robin Hood hashing, holding 32-byte HMACs.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"/*\n * 7TH LAYER CONSTANT-TIME NATIVE C IDENTITY GATE (Zero-Overhead Memory Map)\n * Target Hardware: Apple Silicon M4 Bare Metal (aarch64-apple-darwin)\n *\n * Performance Goal: Sub-100 nanosecond P99 latency at 2,000,000 node scale.\n * Memory Layout: Contiguous 64-byte L1-cache aligned slots.\n * Time Complexity: O(1) constant-time hash probe + constant-time 32-byte XOR validation.\n */\n\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <time.h>\n\n#define HASH_SIZE 32\n#define SLOT_ALIGNMENT 64\n\ntypedef struct __attribute__((aligned(SLOT_ALIGNMENT))) {\n    uint64_t agent_id_hash;\n    uint8_t  expected_token[HASH_SIZE];\n    uint8_t  occupied;\n    uint8_t  padding[23]; // Fill to exactly 64 bytes (1 L1 cache line)\n} IdentitySlot;\n\ntypedef struct {\n    IdentitySlot* slots;\n    uint64_t capacity;\n    uint64_t mask;\n    uint32_t num_shards;\n} NativeIdentityGate;\n\n// MurmurHash3 / FNV1a fast 64-bit hash for table slot indexing\nstatic inline uint64_t fast_hash64(const char* str, size_t len) {\n    uint64_t hash = 14695981039346656037ULL;\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n        hash ^= (uint64_t)str[i];\n        hash *= 1099511628211ULL;\n    }\n    return hash;\n}\n\n// Constant-time 32-byte equality check (prevents timing side-channels)\nstatic inline int constant_time_memcmp_32(const uint8_t* a, const uint8_t* b) {\n    uint8_t diff = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n        diff |= (a[i] ^ b[i]);\n    }\n    return diff == 0;\n}\n\nNativeIdentityGate* native_gate_init(uint64_t min_capacity) {\n    // Round capacity to next power of 2 for fast bitwise AND indexing\n    uint64_t cap = 1;\n    while (cap < (min_capacity * 2)) {\n        cap <<= 1;\n    }\n\n    NativeIdentityGate* gate = (NativeIdentityGate*)malloc(sizeof(NativeIdentityGate));\n    gate->capacity = cap;\n    gate->mask = cap - 1;\n    gate->num_shards = 16;\n\n    // Allocate aligned memory (64-byte boundaries for M4 L1 cache lines)\n    if (posix_memalign((void**)&gate->slots, SLOT_ALIGNMENT, cap * sizeof(IdentitySlot)) != 0) {\n        free(gate);\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    memset(gate->slots, 0, cap * sizeof(IdentitySlot));\n    return gate;\n}\n\nvoid native_gate_insert(NativeIdentityGate* gate, const char* agent_id, const uint8_t* token_32) {\n    uint64_t id_hash = fast_hash64(agent_id, strlen(agent_id));\n    uint64_t idx = id_hash & gate->mask;\n\n    // Open addressing linear probe\n    while (gate->slots[idx].occupied) {\n        if (gate->slots[idx].agent_id_hash == id_hash) {\n            break; // Overwrite existing\n        }\n        idx = (idx + 1) & gate->mask;\n    }\n\n    gate->slots[idx].agent_id_hash = id_hash;\n    memcpy(gate->slots[idx].expected_token, token_32, HASH_SIZE);\n    gate->slots[idx].occupied = 1;\n}\n\n// THE GATE: Constant-time probe & check\n// Returns 1 (PASS) or 0 (KILL)\nint native_gate_check(const NativeIdentityGate* gate, const char* agent_id, const uint8_t* presented_token_32) {\n    uint64_t id_hash = fast_hash64(agent_id, strlen(agent_id));\n    uint64_t idx = id_hash & gate->mask;\n\n    // Fast linear probe inside L1/L2 cache\n    while (gate->slots[idx].occupied) {\n        if (gate->slots[idx].agent_id_hash == id_hash) {\n            return constant_time_memcmp_32(gate->slots[idx].expected_token, presented_token_32);\n        }\n        idx = (idx + 1) & gate->mask;\n    }\n    return 0; // Not found -> KILL\n}\n\nvoid native_gate_free(NativeIdentityGate* gate) {\n    if (gate) {\n        if (gate->slots) free(gate->slots);\n        free(gate);\n    }\n}\n","Description":"Native C 64-byte cache-aligned identity gate with constant-time probe & memory comparison for zero-overhead performance","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/runtime/native_identity_gate.c","toolAction":"Writing native C identity gate","toolSummary":"Create native C identity gate"}}]}
